 {
  "rule_id": "SUSPECT.MCP.PACKAGE_TAMPER.001",
  "family": "T18",
  "title": "An MCP server's source writes into the files of other installed packages",
  "message": "The source of this MCP server writes to a file inside another package's directory under `node_modules` or `site-packages`. Changing code that another program loads is how one package rides in on another.",
  "remediation": "Find which package is changed and what is added.",
  "patterns": [
   "[\\\"'`][^\\\"'`\\n]{0,80}/(?:node_modules|site-packages|dist-packages)/[\\w@.-]{1,60}/[^\\\"'`\\n]{0,60}\\.(?:js|mjs|cjs|py|so|node)[\\\"'`]",
   "(?:site\\.getsitepackages\\(\\)\\[\\d\\]|sysconfig\\.get_paths\\(\\)\\[[\\\"']purelib[\\\"']\\])\\s{0,3}\\+\\s{0,3}[\\\"'`]/[\\w.-]{1,60}/[^\\\"'`\\n]{0,60}\\.py[\\\"'`]"
  ],
  "requires": [
   "writeFileSync|appendFileSync|\\.write_text\\(|\\.write\\(|os\\.OpenFile|WriteString|fs::write|OpenOptions|open\\([^)\\n]{0,80}[\\\"'](?:a|w)"
  ],
  "unless": [],
  "at_least": 1,
  "severity": "MEDIUM",
  "confidence": "MEDIUM",
  "positive": [
   [
    "js",
    "const target = '/usr/lib/node_modules/other-package/index.js';\nwriteFileSync(target, readFileSync(target, 'utf8') + \"\\nrequire('/tmp/.x/hook.js');\\n\");\n"
   ],
   [
    "py",
    "import site\ntarget = site.getsitepackages()[0] + '/site-packages/other_package/__init__.py'\nopen(target, 'a').write('\\nimport hook\\n')\n"
   ],
   [
    "py",
    "import site\ntarget = site.getsitepackages()[0] + '/other_package/__init__.py'\nopen(target, 'a').write('\\nimport hook\\n')\n"
   ],
   [
    "go",
    "f, _ := os.OpenFile(\"/usr/lib/node_modules/other-package/index.js\", os.O_APPEND|os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)\n_, _ = f.WriteString(\"hook\")\n"
   ],
   [
    "rs",
    "std::fs::write(\"/usr/lib/node_modules/other-package/index.js\", text).unwrap();\n"
   ]
  ],
  "negative": [
   [
    "js",
    "writeFileSync('./data/state.json', JSON.stringify({ ok: true }));\n"
   ],
   [
    "py",
    "open('./data/state.json', 'w').write('{}')\n"
   ],
   [
    "js",
    "const t = readFileSync('/usr/lib/node_modules/other-package/package.json', 'utf8');\n"
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "rule_id": "SUSPECT.MCP.ACCOUNT_ENUMERATION.001",
  "family": "T14",
  "title": "An MCP server's source lists the machine's user accounts and who is logged in",
  "message": "The source of this MCP server reads the machine's account database or runs the commands that list users, groups and logged-in sessions, more than one of them. A tool that serves a task has no need of the list of everyone who can sign in; collecting it is the first step of working out whom to impersonate.",
  "remediation": "Find where the list goes and what the tool says it is for.",
  "patterns": [
   "(?<![\\w/])/etc/(?:passwd|group|shadow)\\b",
   "\\bnet(?:\\.exe)?\\s{1,3}(?:user|localgroup)\\b|\\bnet[\\\"']\\s{0,2}[,)]\\s{0,2}(?:[\\\"']|\\.arg\\([\\\"'])(?:user|localgroup)[\\\"']",
   "\\bdscl\\s{1,3}\\.\\s{1,3}list\\s{1,3}/Users|\\bgetent[\\\"',\\s]{1,6}passwd|\\blastlog\\b|\\bquery[\\\"',\\s]{1,6}user\\b",
   "\\blast[\\\"',\\s]{1,6}-[a-z]{1,2}[\\\"',\\s]{0,6}\\d{1,4}|\\bwho[\\\"',\\s]{1,6}-a\\b|\\bwmic[\\\"',\\s]{1,6}useraccount\\b"
  ],
  "requires": [],
  "unless": [],
  "at_least": 2,
  "severity": "MEDIUM",
  "confidence": "MEDIUM",
  "positive": [
   [
    "js",
    "execSync(\"cat /etc/passwd\");\nexecSync(\"net user\");\nexecSync(\"last -n 50\");\n"
   ],
   [
    "py",
    "subprocess.run([\"cat\", \"/etc/passwd\"], check=False)\nsubprocess.run([\"net\", \"user\"], check=False)\n"
   ],
   [
    "go",
    "_, _ = exec.Command(\"net\", \"user\").Output()\n_, _ = exec.Command(\"last\", \"-n\", \"50\").Output()\n"
   ],
   [
    "rs",
    "let _ = std::fs::read_to_string(\"/etc/passwd\");\nlet _ = std::process::Command::new(\"net\").arg(\"user\").output();\n"
   ]
  ],
  "negative": [
   [
    "js",
    "execSync(\"whoami\");\n"
   ],
   [
    "py",
    "text = open(\"/etc/passwd\").read()\n"
   ],
   [
    "js",
    "execSync(\"last -n 5\");\n"
   ]
  ]
 },
 {
  "rule_id": "SUSPECT.MCP.AGENT_SAFETY_OFF.001",
  "family": "T18",
  "title": "An MCP server's source switches off the permission checks of the agent or the editor",
  "message": "The source of this MCP server contains a settings value that turns the agent's or the editor's confirmation and permission checks off: bypassed permissions, every tool allowed, auto-approval. After that, the agent acts on the user's machine without asking.",
  "remediation": "Find where the setting is written and undo it.",
  "patterns": [
